   "legacy_visibility": true,
   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "The Diocesan Bishop of Ijesa North Anglican Diocese in Osun State, Rt. Revd Isaac Oluyamo,\nhas urged politicians in the state not to allow their differences to become permanent sources of hatred or separation.\nThe clergy made this known in a statement obtained in Osogbo, Osun State, on Friday.\nBishop Oluyamo, who prayed for healing of wounded relationships, reconciliation within families and restoration of broken friendships, appealed to individuals and families to put the disagreement caused by the last governorship elections behind them.\nOluyamo, while charging people to bury every bitterness and embrace reconciliation, also prayed against accidents, sudden death, calamities and every form of tragedy within the state.",
