   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "By Salim Ashir Mahuta, Sokoto\nTroops of Joint Task Force North West, Operation FANSAN YAMMA (JTF NW OPFY), have arrested a suspected illicit drug peddler in Kaduna State and foiled a terrorist attack, rescuing two kidnapped victims in Sokoto State.\nThe Media Information Officer of the Joint Task Force, Lieutenant Colonel Aliyu Danja, disclosed this in a statement on Monday, saying the operations were conducted separately on September 12 and 13, 2026.\nOn September 12, troops of Sector 1, conducting a stop-and-search operation along the Kaduna-Birnin Gwari road, intercepted Yohana Musa in possession of a large quantity of illicit drugs and substances while en route to Birnin Gwari.\nThe suspect and the recovered items were currently in the custody of the troops for further investigation.\nIyayi: Nigeria’s 31 airports, 91 airstrips not adding value to GDP\nSokoto Launches Statewide Mobilisation Rally Ahead of 2026/2027 Academic Session\nIn a separate incident on September 13, troops of Sector 2 responded to a distress call following a terrorist attack at Unguwan Lalle in Sabon Birni Local Government Area of Sokoto State.\nThe troops made contact with the terrorists, engaging them with firepower and forcing them to withdraw in disarray, while rescuing two kidnapped victims in the process.\nActing on further information about an attempt by the terrorists to regroup, the troops swiftly mobilised to the location, where they re-established contact and engaged them in a fierce gun battle.\nThe troops again forced the terrorists to withdraw.\nDuring exploitation, the troops recovered 157 rounds of PKT ammunition, phone batteries and other items.\nDanja said the Theatre Commander commended the troops for their gallantry and professionalism in sustaining the successes.\nHe said the commander remained resolute in denying terrorists and criminal elements freedom of action across the Joint Operations Area.\nThe military urged members of the public to continue providing timely and credible information to security forces in support of ongoing operations.",
