   "title_cn": "尼日利亚警察总监视察尼日尔州，承诺彻查37名疑似矿工死亡事件",
   "title_original": "Miners’ deaths: IG visits Niger, promises thorough police investigation",
   "summary_cn": "尼日利亚警察总监奥拉通吉·迪苏前往尼日尔州首府明纳，会见州长乌马尔·巴戈，承诺将彻查37名疑似非法矿工在尼日利亚安全与民防部队羁押期间死亡的事件。迪苏称警方有责任调查羁押期间死亡事件，将与民防部队及州政府合作查明死因。目前该事件为单一来源报道。",
   "summary_original": "The Inspector-General of Police, Olatunji Disu, has visited Niger State and promised a thorough investigation into the deaths of 37 suspected miners. Read More: https://punchng.com/miners-deaths-ig-visits-niger-promises-thorough-police-investigation/",
   "event_time": "2026-09-19T00:46:05Z",
   "published_time": "2026-09-19T00:46:05Z",
   "location": "",
   "china_related": false,
   "verification_level": "single_source",
   "verification_label_cn": "单一来源",
   "independent_source_count": 1,
   "source_links": [
    {
     "url": "https://punchng.com/miners-deaths-ig-visits-niger-promises-thorough-police-investigation/?utm_source=rss.punchng.com&utm_medium=web",
     "source_name": "Punch",
     "source_group": "ng",
     "language": "en"
    }
   ],
   "potential_impact": "",
   "progress": "",
   "current_policy_passed": true,
   "quality_gate_passed": true,
   "legacy_migration_preserved": false,
   "legacy_visibility": true,
   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "The Inspector-General of Police, Olatunji Disu, has visited Niger State Governor Umar Bago and vowed that the police would leave no stone unturned in unraveling the circumstances surrounding the deaths of 37 suspected illegal miners in the custody of the Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps.\nDisu, who arrived at the Niger State Government House in Minna on Friday, said the police would work with the NSCDC and the state government to establish what led to the deaths.\nThe IGP said the police had a responsibility to investigate deaths in custody, describing the incident involving the 37 suspected miners as tragic.\n“I am here this afternoon because of the tragic incident where we lost the lives of 37 citizens of Minna and of this same great state. It is a very tragic incident, and we want to assure you, Your Excellency, that we will leave no stone unturned to unravel the situation that led to these deaths,” he said.",
