   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "The Chief of Defence Staff, Gen. Olufemi Oluyede, has charged the Nigerian Armed Forces to harness emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence and advanced surveillance systems, to improve situational awareness and response to evolving security threats.\nOluyede said this on Friday in Kaduna while inaugurating the Nigerian Defence Academy Command Centre and three other projects at the academy.\nThe other projects were the expanded and remodelled RSM Oliver Nzalgana Parade Ground, the newly constructed 500-capacity Ashanti Battalion Cadets’ Mess and the renovated Ribadu Auditorium.\nThe CDS said the changing nature of contemporary security challenges required the military to continuously adapt and deploy technology to enhance its operational effectiveness.",
