   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "Screengrab: TV Sucesso At least 24 people were killed and two others injured, one of them seriously, in a road accident on Thursday night in Zavala district, southern Mozambique, the Inhambane Provincial Government said on Friday.\nThe accident occurred on National Highway Number 1 (N1).\nIn a statement, shared moments ago on his official Facebook page, Inhambane Governor Francisco Pagula expressed the Provincial Government’s deepest sorrow over the incident and extended heartfelt condolences to the bereaved families, saying the government shared their pain and stood in solidarity with all those suffering at this particularly difficult time.\nAccording to preliminary reports, cited by  Carta de Moçambique , the crash involved a passenger transport vehicle  [chapa]  and a lorry travelling in the opposite direction. The collision caused extensive destruction, with several victims trapped in the wreckage of the passenger vehicle.\nThese reports also indicated that all those killed were travelling in the passenger vehicle. The exact circumstances that led to the collision have yet to be established,  Carta  reports, as the police authorities have not yet officially commented on the accident.\nTV Sucesso, in turn, reporting from the accident scene early this morning, showed two military lorries by the roadside, described by the journalist as an “escolta” allegedly involved in the crash, and reported that the passenger vehicle, with a South African number plate, was travelling from Muxúnguè, in Sofala province, central Mozambique, to South Africa.\nScreengrab: TV Sucesso",
